# Full test suite after refactors

After a **code refactor** (restructuring types, moving packages, extracting classes, or other behavior-preserving edits that touch production or shared test code), you **must** run the **full Maven test matrix** for this repository before treating the work as done. Do not substitute a single `-Dtest=…` class unless the user explicitly asks for a narrower check.

Run from the repo root, in order:

```bash
./mvnw clean test
./mvnw clean test -Psb3
./mvnw clean test -Psb4,tc
```

The last command needs **Docker** (Testcontainers). If Docker is unavailable, say so and run at least the first two; otherwise run all three.

See [TESTING.md](TESTING.md) for profile details.

## JDT workspace sync (mandatory — same session as tests)

The second command above uses **`sb3`**, which switches the Maven classpath and test source roots. **Do not treat the refactor as finished until** you have run the following **after** `./mvnw clean test -Psb3` completes (same agent turn / same session), from the repo root:

```bash
jdt maven update --project spring-data-expresspecs -f
jdt problems --project spring-data-expresspecs
```

Skipping this step is incorrect: Eclipse/JDT will not match Maven until `jdt maven update` runs. Details and rationale: [.cursor/rules/jdt-workspace-sync.mdc](.cursor/rules/jdt-workspace-sync.mdc).

If you also edited `pom.xml` (or other Maven model files this project uses), run the same two commands after those edits as well (even when no `sb3` run occurred).
